--- done — every assertion above passed ---
This confirms: pin the commit for Kev (hash-checking cannot apply to a VCS source;
a 40-character SHA, as install.rs already does, is the only integrity control VCS
requirements support); use a requirements file with --require-hashes and a pinned,
non-latest Laya wheel URL instead of fetching whatever 'releases/latest' currently
resolves to.

Scope: this proves pip/git's own resolution and hash-checking behavior against
synthetic stand-ins. It does not exercise bench/ai-permissions/run.sh itself (its
venv-selection, --rebuild, or per-backend branches), and it does not install the
real Laya or Kev package — see the main report's SUPPLY-001 for what is and is not
claimed from this evidence.

